{
  "summary": "Introduces an AssertUnreachable() macro in util/check.h that directly calls internal_abort_helper with noreturn semantics. Replaces falsy assertions (like assert(false) and Assert(false)) and naked aborts across the codebase using a scripted diff, cleans up dead code following unreachable blocks, and adds an assert_falsy linter rule.",
  "problem": "Unreachable branches guarded by assert(false) or Assert(false) cause toolchain issues: assert(false) triggers warnings under clang-cl and raises confusion regarding NDEBUG behavior, while Assert(false) obscures the noreturn attribute behind a function call and causes -Wreturn-type warnings under GCC. In addition, future use of C++23 std::unreachable() invokes undefined behavior instead of safely aborting.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description links a Compiler Explorer reproducer (https://godbolt.org/z/h7PT3jh3Y) showing -Wreturn-type and unreachable code diagnostics under GCC and clang-cl for the existing patterns."
  ],
